answer.worked:
The new length is $\frac{4}{5}a$ and the new width is $\frac{4}{5}b$.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Area of Copy 1} &= \frac{4}{5}a \times \frac{4}{5}b \\
&= \frac{16ab}{25}
\end{align*}$$

Each copy multiplies the area by $\left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^2 = \frac{16}{25}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Area of Copy } n &= ab\left(\frac{16}{25}\right)^n \\
&= ab\left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^{2n}
\end{align*}$$

